<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Phase 1.8 — what the emulator asks the Hardened Runtime for.

  One entitlement, and it is the one Phase 12 cannot work without: MAP_JIT
  mappings are refused outright unless the binary is signed with this. It is
  requested from Phase 1 rather than Phase 12 so that the signing pipeline is
  proved on an empty application, long before a recompiler is depending on it.

  Deliberately *not* here:

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory — a much blunter
    instrument that disables the protection entirely rather than carving out
    MAP_JIT pages. A JIT that uses pthread_jit_write_protect_np properly does
    not need it, and asking for it would weaken every page in the process.

    com.apple.security.get-task-allow — set by Xcode for debugging, and
    explicitly rejected by the notary service. It must never reach a build
    that is going to be distributed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
